## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a feature into a practical 12‑month CBA with edge constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference costs (latency, energy, memory)
- Privacy and data minimization
- Cloud review costs vs offline results
- Rollout strategy and drift/maintenance costs
- Break-even horizon selection

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateCBA(modelSizeMB, perInferenceJ, inferencesPerMonth, cloudCostPerEvent) {
  const energyKJ = perInferenceJ * inferencesPerMonth;
  const yearlyEnergyCost = (energyKJ / 1000) * 0.9;
  const cloudYear = cloudCostPerEvent * inferencesPerMonth * 12;
  const total = modelSizeMB + yearlyEnergyCost + cloudYear;
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify drift/maintenance costs and retraining cadence?
- How would latency targets influence model size vs accuracy trade-offs?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests the ability to quantify a data-heavy feature with a clear offline-first constraint, balancing device resources against business value.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first architectures
- Local indexing and delta synchronization
- Resource budgeting (CPU, memory, storage)
- Data transfer costs and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```
// Implementation sketch: simple local search index
class LocalIndex {
  constructor() { this.docs = []; }
  build(docs) { this.docs = docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, text: d.content })); }
  search(q) {
    const terms = q.toLowerCase().split(/\s+/);
    return this.docs.filter(d => terms.every(t => d.text.toLowerCase().includes(t)));
  }
  deltaUpdate(changes) {
    // apply lightweight patches to docs
    changes.forEach(c => {
      const idx = this.docs.findIndex(d => d.id === c.id);
      if (idx >= 0) this.docs[idx] = { ...this.docs[idx], ...c.patch };
      else this.docs.push({ id: c.id, text: c.patch.content });
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement delta-sync to minimize data transfer while ensuring consistency?
- What privacy controls would you layer to protect sensitive docs during offline usage?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical cost-benefit thinking for client-side experimentation, balancing latency, data transfer, and privacy across edge and cloud contexts.

## Key Concepts

- Local-first feature flags and variant mapping
- Delta configuration updates and offline resilience
- Privacy, data minimization, and compliance
- Cost modeling: storage, fetch bandwidth, maintenance, and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple config and selection logic
const FLAGS_KEY = 'ab_flags'
function loadFlags(){
  const raw = localStorage.getItem(FLAGS_KEY); return raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : {};
}
function selectVariant(flagName, userHash){
  const flags = loadFlags();
  const flag = flags[flagName];
  if(!flag) return null;
  // deterministic variant from user hash
  const idx = Math.abs(hashCode(userHash + flagName)) % flag.variants.length;
  return flag.variants[idx];
}
function hashCode(s){ let h=0; for(let i=0;i<s.length;i++){ h = (h<<5) - h + s.charCodeAt(i); h |= 0; } return h; }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and handle stale flags in offline mode?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate uplift without compromising privacy?

